course: dictionary
lesson: 9664
title: Substitute: one thing in place of another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A substitute is a person or thing used instead of another. To substitute is to put one thing in the place of another. The words around the word give you the clue: in «substitute 3 for n», the phrase «for n» tells you that 3 takes the place of n.
explain: In sport, a substitute (a «sub») is a player who comes on to replace another player. Read the context: when the coach makes a substitution, the player who comes on is the substitute, and the player who leaves has been replaced.
explain: Look out for the phrases: «substitute A for B», «a substitute for» something, and «come on as a substitute». Try the swap test: put the word «instead» into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A substitute is a person or thing used instead of another.
fact: To substitute is to put one thing in the place of another.
fact: In maths, «substitute 3 for n» means replace n with 3.
fact: A substitute teacher takes the class when the usual teacher is away. In the UK this is called a supply teacher; in Australia, a relief teacher.
fact: «2 soccer teams and 3 basketball teams with no substitutes: 2 × 11 = 22 and 3 × 5 = 15, so 22 + 15 = 37 players.»
exercise: «A substitute or supply teacher deserves the same good behaviour as your usual teacher.» What is a substitute teacher? | *A teacher who takes the class when the usual teacher is away | A teacher who only teaches maths | The head teacher of the whole school
exercise: In maths, what does «substitute 3 for n» mean? | *Replace n with 3 | Add 3 to n | Write n three times
exercise: In sport, what is a «sub»? | A referee who stops the game | *A player who comes on to replace another player | A goal scored at the end of a match
test: To substitute means to do what? | Keep two things together | *Put one thing in the place of another | Count how many things there are | Throw one thing away
test: In «2 × 11 = 22 and 3 × 5 = 15, so 22 + 15 = 37 players», what does 22 + 15 equal? | 42 | 35 | *37 | 27
exam: In the USA, what is a supply teacher called? | *Substitute teacher | Class helper | Head teacher | Relief teacher
